[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/iiPlasma"]
[UTCDate "2018.12.24"]
[UTCTime "01:58:12"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be2 { While the Yugoslav Attack is the ultimate test of the dragon player, the all out win it all or die mentality isn't for everyone. Instead, some might find the Classical variation where white simply developed in a "classical" manner and castles kingside. } 6... Bg7 7. O-O Nc6 8. Be3 { This is a logical move supporting the Knight on d4 but there are a few alternatives.
NOTE: IN the Dragon, Black has many tactics available to exploit from the pressure along the long a1-h8 diagonal. } (8. Bf4 { White neglects to deal with the threat. } 8... Nxe4 9. Nxc6 Qb6 10. Kh1 Nxc3 11. bxc3 bxc6 { Now black has won a critical central pawn from white. }) (8. Nb3 { A more passive move that chooses to bring the knight away from the action in the center. } 8... O-O 9. Bg5 { This is usually the line that white takes to continue with which was made popular by none other than Karpov. (Game 4) }) 8... O-O 9. Nb3 { Once again white is choosing to remove his knight from the center and eliminate any tactics black might have. } (9. Kh1 { If white were to play a waiting move such as this... } 9... d5 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Nxd5 Qxd5 12. Bf3 Qa5 13. Nxc6 bxc6 14. Bxc6 Rb8 { Here we see how Black's pieces are extremly active and his powerful Dragon bishop remains a force to be reckoned with. }) 9... Be6 { Setting up the light square bishop to assist in the future with a queenside attack.
STRATEGIES
White tries to control the center squares (especially d5) with moves like f2-f4-f5 and g2-g4-g5. These thrusts are double edged as white can easily overextend himself and leave counterattack opportunities just waiting for black.
Blacks best hopes of counterplay lie on the semi open c file and the possibility of pushing the a and b pawns. You will also try to get a piece on c4 such as your knight and be looking to see if he can open the position with d6-d5 that would favor him.
The Classical is much more strategic and positional than the Yugoslav. White still focuses on the kingside whereas Black focuses on the queenside but the attacks are more restrained and are more for gaining space than an all out assault on the enemy king. It's also a lot less theoretical and playing good moves based on principle should be more then ample. } *


